    "body": "@karlgroves pointed at the [ARIA design patterns advice](https://www.w3.org/TR/wai-aria-practices-1.1/#dialog_nonmodal) which suggests that it *should* be a tab trap/control group owner, but that the F6 key should (effectively) cycle between the control groups on the page.\r\n\r\nI think that would be ideal, but if we don't implement the cycling between control groups behaviour then the specced behaviour is a tab trap for keyboard users.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
